==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|ecke}}, from {{inh|de|goh|ecka}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*aggju}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*agjō}}. Compare {{cog|en|edge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɛkə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Ecke.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=chen}}

# [[corner]], [[edge]]
#: {{uxi|de|Der Tisch steht in der '''Ecke.'''|The table stands in the '''corner.'''}}
# a roughly [[triangular]] or [[quadrangular]] [[piece]] of something
#: {{ux|de|Gib mir mal eine kleine '''Ecke''' von dem Kuchen.|Give me a small '''piece''' of the cake, please.}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly|colloquial}} [[region]]; [[area]]; [[neighbourhood]]
#: {{ux|de|Ihr wohnt ja hier in ’ner ganz netten '''Ecke.'''|You guys live in a nice '''area''' around here.}}
# {{lb|de|graph theory}} [[vertex]], [[node]]
#: {{syn|de|Knoten}}
# {{lb|de|sports}} [[corner]], [[corner kick]]
#: {{syn|de|Eckball|Eckstoß}}

